{
  "_comment": [
    "Held-out reference corpus for before/after A/B of a rule change.",
    "",
    "NOT the oracle corpus. data/benchmark_repos.json holds the 12 codebases the",
    "ground_truth oracle is adjudicated against; nothing here has labels, a",
    "per-codebase manifest, or a scope predicate, and nothing ever should --",
    "tuning a rule against this set is exactly the overfitting it exists to catch.",
    "",
    "SHADOW SET. Its findings are never imported into ground_truth, never sent",
    "to Postgres, and never reported anywhere -- the one exception is a critical",
    "defect disclosed upstream through the ADR-0007 process. 'bench",
    "realworld-import-labels' refuses any project named here. Selection is for",
    "breadth only: license terms and how receptive upstream is to contributions",
    "were deliberately not criteria.",
    "Every codebase is scanned whole under rules_templates/rules-all.toml.",
    "",
    "Used by 'python -m bench reference-fetch' / 'reference-ab'. Pins were",
    "resolved from each project's latest stable release tag (ref_kind 'tag') or,",
    "where a project tags nothing, its default branch head (ref_kind 'branch').",
    "Re-pinning is free -- no labels depend on these SHAs -- but an A/B is only",
    "comparable between two runs taken at the same pins.",
    "",
    "tier: quick (small, every change), standard, large (slow; opt in).",
    "See docs/design/reference-corpus-ab.md."
  ],
